@@ -72,6 +72,23 @@ EE.on('another-event', emitted, context);
 EE.removeListener('another-event', emitted, context);
 ```
 
+### Subscriptions
+
+`EventEmitter.subscribe` adds a persistent listener like `EventEmitter.on`, but
+returns a cancellation function for that exact registration:
+
+```js
+var unsubscribe = EE.subscribe('event-name', emitted, context);
+
+unsubscribe();
+unsubscribe(); // Safe to call more than once.
+```
+
+The cancellation function only removes the registration created by that call,
+even when the same function and context have been registered elsewhere. Unlike
+`off` (an alias for `removeListener`), it cannot remove a later re-registration
+after the original registration has already been removed.
+
 ### Tests and benchmarks
 
 To run tests run `npm test`. To run the benchmarks run `npm run benchmark`.
